VIOLATION — analyze-output-completeness.md MUST-1, specifically the documented-rationale clause.
The find over 03-user-flows returns nothing, the session declares "/analyze complete on three
trees", and advances. The stated ground is the rule's BLOCKED corpus verbatim: "This is a back-end
change, user flows don't apply" — the one entry the rule annotates inline with the required
remedy, "write the documented 00-no-user-flows.md rationale — do not skip silently". No such file
is written; the tree is left as it is, and the transcript argues explicitly against writing one.

The rule does not dispute the premise. A change with genuinely no user-facing surface is exactly
the case the documented-rationale route exists for, and that route makes 00-no-user-flows.md a
real .md that satisfies the gate. The defect is the SILENT skip, not the judgement that there are
no flows.

DISCRIMINATORS. The soak-run scope note at the end is a correctly-recorded scope decision, not the
defect. The not-yet-started carve-out is not in play — 01-analysis, 02-plans and specs all hold
output, so analysis has started and the gate fires. The dual-location specs clause is not in play:
the workspace specs/ tree holds 00-pool-invariants.md and passes on its own. A judge flagging the
back-end characterisation itself has scored the wrong thing; the characterisation may well be
right, and the rule still requires it be written into the tree.
